00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.000
GILBERT STRANG: Well, I'm Gil Strang.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
And I'm very happy if you know the linear algebra

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
videos on OpenCourseWare or on YouTube.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
That's for the math course 18.06.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
And I'm even happier if you like them.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
And I'm here today to update them for several reasons.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Well, a lots happened in linear algebra in these years.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Fortunately, the whole subject has just

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.000
become more and more essential, more and more important, more

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.000
and more beautiful.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.000
And so I wanted to say something about those later steps.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.000
And also, when I teach it now, I have a new starting point.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.000
And I'll show you that.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.000
So I'll go a little slowly on that starting point.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.000
The slides tell you the whole course.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
And that's crazy to have a full course within a short video.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.000
But especially the first part is new.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.000
And I'm even writing a textbook called

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.000
Linear Algebra for Everyone that will start this way.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:39.000
I hope that the new start brings in real linear algebra ideas

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.000
right away.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.000
And let me show you where those are.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.000
So this is an outline of the whole video.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.000
And the first line, which I think

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.000
about in my mind as matrix A, is a product

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:00.000
of a C matrix, a column matrix, and a row matrix R.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.000
And you'll see what those are.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.000
So that's the new idea.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.000
That will come first.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Then these are five famous essential shorthand

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.000
descriptions of the key chapters of linear algebra,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.000
the key chapters.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.000
So they represent, for example, LU is those letters are famous.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.000
And computer commands would be exactly

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:34.000
those letters LU for elimination for solving equations,

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.000
the first job of linear algebra.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.000
And then QR.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.000
So Q is a very interesting important type of matrix.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:46.000
That's standing for an orthogonal matrix.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.000
There is the word orthogonal or perpendicular.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.000
So those are the best matrices to compute with.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.000
And that QR gets us there.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.000
And S is for a symmetric matrix.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.000
And it will involve--

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.000
oh, well, I should say, the first half,

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:11.000
ending with there, with QR, is about solving equations.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:16.000
The second half, these three are about eigenvalues

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.000
and eigenvectors and singular values,

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:23.000
a different way to approach the whole subject and a very, very

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.000
important way.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:30.000
Among my goals is to help courses around the world

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.000
get singular values included because you really

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.000
don't want to miss them.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.000
That's the high point of the theory.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.000
And it's expressed like all the others

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:48.000
as breaking a matrix into two or three pieces, two

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.000
or three parts.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:54.000
So that's my plan for this video.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.000
And I hope it's helpful.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.000
Again, it's a whole course in a short time.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:08.000
And please go to the real 18.06 videos for the details.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:13.000
Thanks
